cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "beam-target"
abstract: >-
  Neutron source terms for beam-target neutron generators, for MCNP and OpenMC. A beam of
  protons, deuterons, tritons, 3He, or alphas slows down through gas or solid target regions,
  with beam divergence, wall scraping, and losses to nuclear reactions; neutrons come from the
  built-in DROSG-2000 two-body reactions or from evaluated nuclear data libraries in ENDF-6
  format, converted to the lab frame with relativistic kinematics. The source is written as an
  MCNP SDEF card, OpenMC sources, and an HDF5 file.
authors:
  - given-names: Lucas
    family-names: Jacobson
    affiliation: "SHINE Technologies, LLC"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lucasjacobson/beam-target"
keywords:
  - neutron source
  - neutron generator
  - beam-target
  - MCNP
  - OpenMC
  - fusion
  - nuclear data
